1
00:00:35,502 --> 00:00:40,423
HARRY POTTER AND THE ORDER OF THE PHOENIX

2
00:01:02,821 --> 00:01:05,615
<i>It's very hot today, isn't it?</i>

3
00:01:05,782 --> 00:01:10,120
<i>And he is going to do even more.
Temperatures in the 30s Celsius...</i>

4
00:01:10,286 --> 00:01:13,998
<i>...which is 90 degrees Fahrenheit
tomorrow, maybe up to 100.</i>

5
00:01:14,165 --> 00:01:16,835
<i>Remember to cover up and cool off...</i>

6
00:01:17,001 --> 00:01:19,838
<i>...with the best musical hits.</i>

7
00:01:20,004 --> 00:01:22,632
come! Let's go home.

8
00:01:23,508 --> 00:01:25,635
Come on, sweetheart, get off.

9
00:01:27,595 --> 00:01:31,015
- Do we have to go?
- Yes, yes we have.

10
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:34,561
I will prepare your favorite dinner.

11
00:01:35,937 --> 00:01:37,605
He squealed like a pig, didn't he?

12
00:01:37,772 --> 00:01:41,234
Yeah, nice shot, Big D.
Did you see his face?

13
00:01:41,484 --> 00:01:43,319
Hello, Big D.

14
00:01:44,154 --> 00:01:45,655
Did you hit another ten year old?

15
00:01:45,822 --> 00:01:48,199
This one deserved it.

16
00:01:48,992 --> 00:01:53,329
- Five against one, how brave.
- Look who says it.

17
00:01:53,496 --> 00:01:58,501
You moan in your sleep every night.
I'm not afraid of my pillow.

18
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,715
"Don't kill Cedric!"

19
00:02:04,215 --> 00:02:06,384
Who is Cedric, your boyfriend?

20
00:02:07,177 --> 00:02:11,139
- Shut up.
- "He's going to kill me, mom!"

21
00:02:11,639 --> 00:02:13,349
Where is your mom?

22
00:02:14,851 --> 00:02:17,270
Where is your mother, Potter?

23
00:02:17,687 --> 00:02:19,189
Is she dead?

24
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:22,358
Is she dead?

25
00:02:23,026 --> 00:02:24,527
Is she a dead Potter?

26
00:02:43,129 --> 00:02:44,964
- What's wrong?
- What are you doing?

27
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:48,092
- I'm not doing anything!
- Let's go, Dudley!

28
00:03:40,061 --> 00:03:42,021
Dudley, run!

29
00:04:17,765 --> 00:04:19,601
<i>Expecto patronum!</i>

30
00:04:49,005 --> 00:04:50,798
Mrs. Figg.

31
00:04:54,677 --> 00:04:56,721
Don't put away your wand, Harry.

32
00:04:57,221 --> 00:04:59,349
They can return.

33
00:05:00,725 --> 00:05:03,728
Dementors in Little Whinging?
What's next?

34
00:05:03,978 --> 00:05:07,815
- The world is upside down.
- I don't understand. How do you know about...?

35
00:05:07,982 --> 00:05:10,318
Dumbledore asked me to keep an eye on you.

36
00:05:10,485 --> 00:05:13,488
Dumbledore? Do you know Dumbledore?

37
00:05:13,863 --> 00:05:17,867
After You-Know-Who
He killed the Diggory boy...

38
00:05:18,034 --> 00:05:20,578
...did you expect me to leave you
walk at ease?

39
00:05:20,745 --> 00:05:24,332
Gosh, boy.
They told me you were smart.

40
00:05:24,499 --> 00:05:26,668
Go into the house and stay there.

41
00:05:26,834 --> 00:05:31,422
Someone will contact you.
Don't leave the house.

42
00:05:40,973 --> 00:05:43,351
<i>It's hot. Yes, it's hot everywhere.</i>

43
00:05:43,518 --> 00:05:45,812
<i>You sweat, you suffocate.</i>

44
00:05:45,978 --> 00:05:47,730
Puppy?

45
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:49,982
Is it you?

46
00:05:53,277 --> 00:05:56,406
Duddy.
Vernon, come quickly!

47
00:05:57,198 --> 00:05:59,617
We have to take him to the hospital.

48
00:05:59,784 --> 00:06:01,911
Who did this to you, boy?

49
00:06:06,082 --> 00:06:08,084
Are we happy yet?

50
00:06:09,335 --> 00:06:12,213
You finally did it.
You finally drove him crazy.

51
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:15,049
Vernon, don't say that!

52
00:06:15,425 --> 00:06:19,595
Look at it, Petunia! Our son went crazy!

53
00:06:19,971 --> 00:06:21,931
I can't take it anymore, do you hear me?

54
00:06:22,265 --> 00:06:26,102
I'm not going to tolerate you anymore
to you or your nonsense.

55
00:06:39,991 --> 00:06:42,034
Dear Mr. Potter,

56
00:06:42,285 --> 00:06:47,498
The Ministry received information
that at 6:23 this afternoon...

57
00:06:47,665 --> 00:06:52,336
...you performed the enchantment
patronus in front of a muggle.

58
00:06:52,628 --> 00:06:55,715
This being a clear
violation of the decree...

59
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:58,926
...for the moderate limitation of witchcraft
in minors...

60
00:06:59,093 --> 00:07:01,345
...he is expelled...

61
00:07:01,679 --> 00:07:05,057
...from Hogwarts School
of Magic and Sorcery.

62
00:07:05,725 --> 00:07:09,729
Waiting for it to be found
well, Mafalda Hopkirk.

63
00:07:14,192 --> 00:07:16,235
Justice.

64
00:07:43,513 --> 00:07:45,473
Sorry, Hedwig.

65
00:08:52,665 --> 00:08:54,417
These muggles are very clean.

66
00:08:54,625 --> 00:08:57,295
- Tonks, for God's sake.
- It's not natural.

67
00:09:01,465 --> 00:09:03,175
Professor Moody.

68
00:09:03,676 --> 00:09:06,637
- What are you doing here?
- Rescuing you, of course.

69
00:09:09,765 --> 00:09:12,268
Where are we going?
I was expelled from Hogwarts.

70
00:09:12,435 --> 00:09:15,021
Not yet.
Kingsley, go toe.

71
00:09:15,187 --> 00:09:16,147
But the letter said...

72
00:09:16,314 --> 00:09:19,901
Dumbledore convinced the minister
to give you an audience.

73
00:09:20,276 --> 00:09:21,611
An audience?

74
00:09:21,777 --> 00:09:25,156
We will explain everything to you
in the operations center.

75
00:09:25,323 --> 00:09:27,617
Not here. Nymphadora!

76
00:09:27,783 --> 00:09:31,454
Don't call me Nymphadora.

77
00:09:36,959 --> 00:09:41,047
Stay in formation.
Do not separate even if one dies.

78
00:10:34,976 --> 00:10:36,435
Let's go.

79
00:11:15,808 --> 00:11:17,435
Come in, son.

80
00:11:22,732 --> 00:11:25,609
He almost killed Harry.

81
00:11:25,776 --> 00:11:29,739
Yes, but protect you know
what is the most important thing.

82
00:11:31,991 --> 00:11:34,410
You have to trust Dumbledore.

83
00:11:34,577 --> 00:11:38,998
Did you protect Harry last year?
It's time to take action.

84
00:11:39,165 --> 00:11:42,376
Cornelius Fudge is a politician
first, then a magician.

85
00:11:42,543 --> 00:11:45,713
- Your instinct is to ignore it...
-Lower your voice!

86
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:50,092
It's getting stronger every minute.
We must act now!

87
00:11:54,263 --> 00:11:56,599
-Harry.
- Mrs. Weasley.

88
00:11:59,226 --> 00:12:01,562
Gosh, you're fine!

89
00:12:05,232 --> 00:12:08,944
You are skinny, but we will have
to have dinner after the meeting.

90
00:12:09,111 --> 00:12:14,283
There is no time to explain it to you.
Up and to the left.

91
00:12:18,329 --> 00:12:23,459
Mudblood and men
wolf and traitors and thieves.

92
00:12:23,709 --> 00:12:28,589
If my poor mistress knew the rubbish
who enters this house...

93
00:12:28,756 --> 00:12:30,966
...what would you say to old Kreacher?

94
00:12:32,093 --> 00:12:34,762
Oh, what a shame.

95
00:12:47,483 --> 00:12:50,152
- Abnormal.
- Calm down, calm down, love.

96
00:12:50,319 --> 00:12:53,781
<i>Pure scum. not like
in my parents' times.</i>

97
00:12:53,989 --> 00:12:55,741
Kreacher is here.

98
00:13:00,663 --> 00:13:02,081
Oh, Harry!

99
00:13:04,792 --> 00:13:08,712
Are you okay? we hear them
talk about the attack of the dementors.

100
00:13:08,879 --> 00:13:11,715
- You have to tell us everything.
- Let him breathe, Hermione.

101
00:13:11,882 --> 00:13:15,970
And that hearing at the Ministry.
It's a scandal!

102
00:13:16,137 --> 00:13:18,430
I already investigated and they can't expel you.

103
00:13:18,597 --> 00:13:20,724
It's unfair.

104
00:13:21,809 --> 00:13:24,436
There have been many injustices.

105
00:13:26,355 --> 00:13:28,274
What is this place?

106
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:31,402
- The operations center.
- From the Order of the Phoenix.

107
00:13:31,777 --> 00:13:33,445
It's a secret society.

108
00:13:33,612 --> 00:13:36,198
Dumbledore formed her the first time
They fought against You-Know-Who.

109
00:13:36,365 --> 00:13:38,993
And couldn't they have written to me?

110
00:13:39,577 --> 00:13:41,620
I didn't have any news all summer.

111
00:13:42,371 --> 00:13:46,041
We wanted to write to you, friend.
Really.

112
00:13:46,208 --> 00:13:47,209
- But...
- But what?

113
00:13:47,376 --> 00:13:50,296
Dumbledore made us swear
not tell you anything.

114
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:53,883
Did Dumbledore say that?

115
00:13:55,718 --> 00:13:58,637
Why didn't he want me to find out?
I could have helped them.

116
00:13:58,804 --> 00:14:00,931
I saw Voldemort return.

117
00:14:01,098 --> 00:14:03,601
I fought against him, I saw him die
to Cedric Diggory.

118
00:14:03,809 --> 00:14:06,145
We thought we heard your melodious voice.

119
00:14:06,312 --> 00:14:10,399
- Express your feelings. Take them out.
- If they're done screaming...

120
00:14:10,691 --> 00:14:12,902
...do you want to hear something more interesting?

121
00:14:14,153 --> 00:14:17,698
<i>If anyone has a right to know, it's Harry.
If it weren't for him...</i>

122
00:14:17,865 --> 00:14:19,909
<i>...we wouldn't know that Voldemort has returned.</i>

123
00:14:20,075 --> 00:14:21,660
He's not a boy, Molly.

124
00:14:21,827 --> 00:14:24,038
<i>He is not an adult either.</i>

125
00:14:24,371 --> 00:14:27,416
- It's not<i>James, Sirius.
- And he's not your son.</i>

126
00:14:27,625 --> 00:14:29,543
<i>It almost is.</i>

127
00:14:30,002 --> 00:14:32,755
<i>- Who else do you have?
- He has me.</i>

128
00:14:32,922 --> 00:14:34,423
<i>How fatherly, you move me.</i>

129
00:14:34,590 --> 00:14:37,718
<i>Maybe Harry will become a criminal,
like you.</i>

130
00:14:37,968 --> 00:14:39,637
<i>Stay out, Whimper.</i>

131
00:14:39,803 --> 00:14:42,723
- Does Snape belong to the Order?
- Disgraceful.

132
00:14:44,099 --> 00:14:46,810
<i>- I know not.
- Why don't you tell him?</i>

133
00:14:46,977 --> 00:14:48,479
Stop that!

134
00:14:48,771 --> 00:14:50,397
- Pick it up!
- Crookshanks!

135
00:14:50,648 --> 00:14:53,067
- Enough.
- Leave it, damn cat!

136
00:14:53,234 --> 00:14:55,819
Crookshanks! Leave him alone!

137
00:14:57,446 --> 00:15:01,116
- Hermione, I hate your cat.
- Bad Crookshanks!

138
00:15:02,952 --> 00:15:04,870
Let's eat in the kitchen.

139
00:15:06,247 --> 00:15:08,290
Just because they can already use magic...

140
00:15:08,457 --> 00:15:11,502
...they don't have to take out their wands for everything!

141
00:15:14,255 --> 00:15:15,965
Are you hungry, Harry?

142
00:15:16,131 --> 00:15:18,801
Are you sure you're okay?
You gave us a good scare.

143
00:15:18,968 --> 00:15:21,136
Harry Potter.

144
00:15:23,305 --> 00:15:25,140
Sirius!

145
00:15:30,688 --> 00:15:33,148
This is very, very peculiar.

146
00:15:33,315 --> 00:15:36,986
It seems that your audience
It will be first and foremost the Wizengamot.

147
00:15:37,152 --> 00:15:40,406
What does the Ministry have
of Magic against me?

148
00:15:41,490 --> 00:15:44,493
Teach him.
Maybe he'll find out soon.

149
00:15:53,919 --> 00:15:55,129
THE BOY WHO LIES?

150
00:15:55,296 --> 00:15:58,340
It has also been attacking
to Dumbledore.

151
00:15:58,507 --> 00:16:00,009
FUDGE: "EVERYTHING IS WELL."

152
00:16:00,175 --> 00:16:05,097
Fudge is using his power, including
his influence on The Prophet...

153
00:16:05,347 --> 00:16:08,475
...against those who say
that the Dark Lord has returned.

154
00:16:08,642 --> 00:16:11,937
- Why?
-He thinks Dumbledore wants to replace him.

155
00:16:12,104 --> 00:16:14,356
But no one who is
In his right mind he can believe...

156
00:16:14,523 --> 00:16:17,401
Exactly. Fudge is not in his right mind.

157
00:16:17,568 --> 00:16:19,903
Fear has distorted your mind.

158
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:24,199
Fear leads us to do terrible things.

159
00:16:24,366 --> 00:16:26,827
The last time Voldemort
acquired power...

160
00:16:26,994 --> 00:16:30,205
...almost destroys everything we love most.

161
00:16:30,372 --> 00:16:34,293
Now it's back. I'm afraid
that the minister will do whatever...

162
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:37,379
...to not face that terrifying truth.

163
00:16:38,797 --> 00:16:43,093
We think Voldemort wants to come back
to build his army.

164
00:16:44,595 --> 00:16:47,264
14 years ago I had a huge army...

165
00:16:47,431 --> 00:16:51,393
...of witches, wizards
and many dark beings.

166
00:16:52,728 --> 00:16:56,565
He has been recruiting many,
and so do we.

167
00:16:57,566 --> 00:17:01,236
But he is not only interested
get more followers.

168
00:17:04,281 --> 00:17:05,866
We believe...

169
00:17:07,076 --> 00:17:08,994
...that Voldemort wants to get something.

170
00:17:09,203 --> 00:17:10,913
Sirius.

171
00:17:13,957 --> 00:17:16,752
Something I didn't have last time.

172
00:17:18,295 --> 00:17:20,255
Something like a weapon?

173
00:17:20,506 --> 00:17:24,426
No. Enough.
He's just a boy.

174
00:17:24,635 --> 00:17:27,554
If you say more, you'll have to admit it
to the Order immediately.

175
00:17:27,721 --> 00:17:31,517
Perfect! If Voldemort is
building an army, I want to fight.

176
00:17:43,987 --> 00:17:45,864
<i>Harry!</i>

177
00:17:46,031 --> 00:17:48,283
<i>You are expelled!</i>

178
00:17:48,450 --> 00:17:50,786
<i>First and foremost the Wizengamot.</i>

179
00:18:00,421 --> 00:18:02,381
Trains. One meter.

180
00:18:02,548 --> 00:18:04,842
How clever muggles are.

181
00:18:22,025 --> 00:18:23,777
We're here.

182
00:18:25,529 --> 00:18:29,992
I have never used the visitor entrance.
It's going to be fun.

183
00:18:30,826 --> 00:18:35,038
Good. Let me get my muggle money.

184
00:19:15,078 --> 00:19:18,081
Yesterday I had a terrible day.
I lost a lot of galleons in the stock market.

185
00:19:18,248 --> 00:19:21,543
<i>The Prophet. Does anyone want The Prophet?</i>

186
00:19:21,710 --> 00:19:24,546
Dumbledore: Mad or dangerous?

187
00:19:46,693 --> 00:19:49,488
- Good morning, Arthur.
- Good morning, Bob.

188
00:19:51,907 --> 00:19:53,700
Interdepartmental memoranda.

189
00:19:53,867 --> 00:19:57,663
Before we used owls. It was disgusting.

190
00:20:02,751 --> 00:20:05,921
By Merlin's beard.
Thanks, Kingsley.

191
00:20:06,588 --> 00:20:09,675
- They changed the time of your hearing.
- When is it?

192
00:20:10,342 --> 00:20:12,219
In five minutes.

193
00:20:19,893 --> 00:20:23,105
<i>Department of Mysteries.</i>

194
00:20:25,649 --> 00:20:29,778
And I have full confidence
that you will do the right thing.

195
00:20:29,945 --> 00:20:32,489
Yes, but we must be...

196
00:20:39,204 --> 00:20:42,499
During the hearing,
Speak only when spoken to.

197
00:20:42,791 --> 00:20:46,003
Stay calm.
You haven't done anything wrong.

198
00:20:46,753 --> 00:20:49,756
As the muggles say,
the truth will triumph.

199
00:20:50,424 --> 00:20:51,800
Yes?

200
00:20:52,634 --> 00:20:55,012
I'm afraid I can't get in.

201
00:20:56,888 --> 00:20:58,640
Good luck, Harry.

202
00:21:02,603 --> 00:21:05,147
Disciplinary hearing on August 12...

203
00:21:05,314 --> 00:21:07,858
...offenses committed
by Harry James Potter...

204
00:21:08,025 --> 00:21:12,029
...resident of Privet Drive
Number Four, Little Whinging.

205
00:21:12,195 --> 00:21:15,324
Questioners:
Cornelius Oswald Fudge, Minister...

206
00:21:15,490 --> 00:21:17,326
Defense witness!

207
00:21:17,492 --> 00:21:20,537
Albus Percival Wulfric...

208
00:21:20,829 --> 00:21:24,374
...Brian Dumbledore.

209
00:21:24,666 --> 00:21:27,878
Did you get the message that they changed...

210
00:21:28,045 --> 00:21:30,672
- ...the time and place?
- I think I missed it.

211
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:34,718
But by a lucky mistake,
I arrived three hours early.

212
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:38,847
The charges?

213
00:21:39,014 --> 00:21:41,683
The charges against the accused
are the following:

214
00:21:41,850 --> 00:21:43,477
«That knowingly...

215
00:21:43,644 --> 00:21:47,189
...and knowing the illegality of his actions...

216
00:21:47,356 --> 00:21:50,359
...performed a patronus charm...

217
00:21:50,525 --> 00:21:53,654
...in the presence of a muggle.

218
00:21:53,862 --> 00:21:57,240
- Do you deny having produced a patronus?
- No. But...

219
00:21:57,407 --> 00:22:00,869
Did you know you can't use magic
outside of school...

220
00:22:01,036 --> 00:22:03,914
- ...being under 17 years old?
- Yes, I knew it, but...

221
00:22:04,081 --> 00:22:07,209
Witches and wizards of the Wizengamot...

222
00:22:07,376 --> 00:22:09,711
I only did it for the dementors!

223
00:22:12,589 --> 00:22:14,216
Dementors?

224
00:22:14,841 --> 00:22:16,551
In Little Whinging?

225
00:22:16,718 --> 00:22:18,595
How ingenious.

226
00:22:19,221 --> 00:22:22,265
Muggles can't see dementors,
right, boy?

227
00:22:22,599 --> 00:22:24,726
- How convenient.
- I'm not lying!

228
00:22:24,893 --> 00:22:27,312
-There were two and if there weren't...
- Enough!

229
00:22:27,646 --> 00:22:31,858
I'm sorry to interrupt what you had
It's been a well-rehearsed story...

230
00:22:32,025 --> 00:22:36,363
...but since you can't present
a witness to the event...

231
00:22:36,530 --> 00:22:40,867
Forgive me, Mr. Minister.
But it turns out that we can.

232
00:22:44,621 --> 00:22:47,624
Please describe the attack.

233
00:22:50,502 --> 00:22:52,254
What did they look like?

234
00:22:54,798 --> 00:22:58,218
One of them was very big
and the other quite skinny.

235
00:22:59,428 --> 00:23:02,222
Not the boys, the dementors.

236
00:23:02,389 --> 00:23:05,976
Oh, right, right. Well, they were big.

237
00:23:07,269 --> 00:23:08,478
They brought capes.

238
00:23:08,645 --> 00:23:11,773
Then it was very cold...

239
00:23:12,482 --> 00:23:15,902
...as if all the happiness
from the world would have disappeared.

240
00:23:16,069 --> 00:23:21,158
Look, dementors don't get lost
in a muggle suburb...

241
00:23:21,324 --> 00:23:25,078
...and they run into a wizard.
The odds are astronomical.

242
00:23:25,287 --> 00:23:26,872
I don't think anyone thinks...

243
00:23:27,038 --> 00:23:29,624
...that were there by chance.

244
00:23:32,627 --> 00:23:35,464
Surely I misunderstood, professor.

245
00:23:35,630 --> 00:23:41,136
Dementors are controlled
by the Ministry of Magic.

246
00:23:41,303 --> 00:23:45,515
It's absurd, but it seemed to me
for a second...

247
00:23:45,682 --> 00:23:49,686
...that you were suggesting that the Ministry
He ordered the attack on the boy.

248
00:23:49,853 --> 00:23:52,647
Which would be very disturbing,
Madam Undersecretary.

249
00:23:52,814 --> 00:23:56,985
I am sure that the Ministry
will do an investigation...

250
00:23:57,152 --> 00:24:00,322
...about why there were two dementors
so far from Azkaban...

251
00:24:00,697 --> 00:24:03,909
...and why they rode
an unauthorized attack.

252
00:24:04,826 --> 00:24:07,037
Of course there is someone...

253
00:24:07,454 --> 00:24:09,956
...which may be behind the attack.

254
00:24:13,126 --> 00:24:17,506
Cornelius, I implore you to be reasonable.

255
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:22,511
The evidence that the Dark Lord
has returned is incontrovertible.

256
00:24:22,677 --> 00:24:25,222
He hasn't come back!

257
00:24:31,144 --> 00:24:33,522
On the matter of Harry Potter...

258
00:24:33,980 --> 00:24:35,982
...the law says...

259
00:24:36,775 --> 00:24:38,860
...that you can use magic
in front of muggles...

260
00:24:39,027 --> 00:24:41,196
...in life-threatening situations.

261
00:24:41,363 --> 00:24:44,241
Laws can be changed
if necessary.

262
00:24:44,407 --> 00:24:47,577
Obviously. Has it turned
custom to make criminal trials...

263
00:24:47,744 --> 00:24:50,705
...to deal with issues
of minor magic?

264
00:24:59,047 --> 00:25:02,509
Those in favor of condemning?

265
00:25:11,393 --> 00:25:16,147
Those in favor of exonerating
to the accused of all charges?

266
00:25:30,370 --> 00:25:32,581
Exonerated of all charges.

267
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:37,502
Professor!

268
00:25:50,348 --> 00:25:53,476
Padfoot! Are you crazy rabid?

269
00:25:53,810 --> 00:25:55,854
You'll disrupt the entire operation!

270
00:26:04,446 --> 00:26:07,115
Sirius, what are you doing here? If they see you...

271
00:26:07,282 --> 00:26:09,784
I had to say goodbye, right?

272
00:26:11,578 --> 00:26:13,955
What is life without risks?

273
00:26:14,623 --> 00:26:16,708
I don't want them to send you to Azkaban.

274
00:26:16,875 --> 00:26:18,168
Don't worry about me.

275
00:26:18,793 --> 00:26:23,673
Anyway, I wanted to give you this.

276
00:26:29,095 --> 00:26:32,015
The original Order of the Phoenix.

277
00:26:32,641 --> 00:26:34,476
Marlene McKinnon.

278
00:26:34,643 --> 00:26:37,020
They killed her for two weeks
after this photo.

279
00:26:37,354 --> 00:26:40,732
Voldemort wiped out his entire family.

280
00:26:41,066 --> 00:26:42,817
Frank and Alice Longbottom.

281
00:26:43,026 --> 00:26:44,361
Neville's parents.

282
00:26:44,527 --> 00:26:48,365
They suffered a worse fate
than death, I say.

283
00:26:50,325 --> 00:26:52,786
That was 14 years ago.

284
00:26:53,495 --> 00:26:57,666
And still not a day passes
that I don't miss your dad.

285
00:27:02,504 --> 00:27:05,757
Do you really think there is going to be war?

286
00:27:07,676 --> 00:27:10,804
It looks like last time.

287
00:27:15,016 --> 00:27:16,559
Stay with her.

288
00:27:17,352 --> 00:27:21,648
I guess you guys are the young ones now.

289
00:28:19,372 --> 00:28:22,083
I am surprised that the Ministry
has set you free.

290
00:28:22,250 --> 00:28:23,918
Enjoy it while you can.

291
00:28:24,085 --> 00:28:27,213
I think there is a cell in Azkaban
with your name.

292
00:28:30,008 --> 00:28:33,970
- What did I tell you? He's crazy!
- Don't come near me!

293
00:28:35,180 --> 00:28:37,015
It's just Malfoy.

294
00:28:37,849 --> 00:28:39,517
What did you expect?

295
00:28:59,662 --> 00:29:00,830
Hello, friends.

296
00:29:00,997 --> 00:29:02,582
Hello, Neville.

297
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,263
What is that?

298
00:29:19,432 --> 00:29:22,685
- What?
- That. What pulls the carriage.

299
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:25,772
Nothing is pulling the float.

300
00:29:26,481 --> 00:29:28,650
She goes alone, as always.

301
00:29:42,330 --> 00:29:44,499
You're not going crazy.

302
00:29:47,127 --> 00:29:49,295
I see them too.

303
00:29:50,630 --> 00:29:53,049
You are as sane as I am.

304
00:29:58,012 --> 00:30:00,098
I present to you Lunatica Love...

305
00:30:02,892 --> 00:30:04,811
Luna Lovegood.

306
00:30:08,731 --> 00:30:10,733
What an interesting necklace.

307
00:30:11,609 --> 00:30:13,778
It's an amulet.

308
00:30:15,155 --> 00:30:16,698
Drive away the nargles.

309
00:30:20,535 --> 00:30:21,911
I'm hungry.

310
00:30:22,704 --> 00:30:24,581
I hope there's pudding.

311
00:30:25,665 --> 00:30:29,085
- What is a nargle?
- I have no idea.

312
00:30:41,890 --> 00:30:43,474
Good night, children!

313
00:30:44,893 --> 00:30:47,604
We have two personnel changes this year.

314
00:30:47,770 --> 00:30:50,815
Let's receive again
to Professor Grubbly-Plank...

315
00:30:50,982 --> 00:30:53,568
...who will teach Care
of Magical Creatures...

316
00:30:53,735 --> 00:30:57,113
...while Professor Hagrid is away.

317
00:30:58,031 --> 00:31:02,035
And let's receive the teacher
Defense Against the Dark Arts...

318
00:31:02,202 --> 00:31:04,954
...Professor Dolores Umbridge.

319
00:31:05,663 --> 00:31:09,334
I'm sure everyone
We wish you good luck.

320
00:31:10,210 --> 00:31:14,547
As always, our caretaker,
Mr. Filch wants to remind you...

321
00:31:26,100 --> 00:31:29,020
He was in my audience.
He works for Fudge.

322
00:31:29,187 --> 00:31:34,108
Thank you, Mr. Director,
for your kind words of welcome.

323
00:31:36,277 --> 00:31:39,948
And how lovely to see their brilliant...

324
00:31:40,114 --> 00:31:42,951
...happy faces smiling at me.

325
00:31:43,284 --> 00:31:48,498
I'm sure we all go
to be very good friends.

326
00:31:48,831 --> 00:31:50,792
It is very likely.

327
00:31:53,670 --> 00:31:56,714
The Ministry of Magic
has always considered...

328
00:31:56,881 --> 00:32:02,387
...education is of utmost importance
of young witches and wizards.

329
00:32:02,679 --> 00:32:09,644
Although each director has contributed
something new to this historic school...

330
00:32:11,688 --> 00:32:17,777
...progress in name only
of progress must be discouraged.

331
00:32:18,403 --> 00:32:22,156
Let's preserve what must be preserved...

332
00:32:22,407 --> 00:32:25,952
...let's perfect
what can be perfected...

333
00:32:26,244 --> 00:32:32,667
...and let's eliminate practices
that should be prohibited.

334
00:32:39,757 --> 00:32:44,012
Thank you, Professor Umbridge.
That was very enlightening.

335
00:32:44,178 --> 00:32:48,391
- Enlightening? What a bunch of nonsense.
- What does it mean?

336
00:32:51,644 --> 00:32:55,148
It means that the Ministry
is interfering at Hogwarts.

337
00:33:07,869 --> 00:33:09,454
POTTER PLOTS?

338
00:33:15,001 --> 00:33:16,627
Dean, Seamus.

339
00:33:16,878 --> 00:33:19,047
- Good vacation?
- Pretty good.

340
00:33:19,380 --> 00:33:21,716
Better than Seamus's.

341
00:33:22,842 --> 00:33:25,178
My mom didn't want me to come back this year.

342
00:33:25,345 --> 00:33:28,806
- Why not?
- Let me see. For you.

343
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:32,894
The Prophet has been speaking
a lot of you and Dumbledore.

344
00:33:33,061 --> 00:33:34,187
And your mom believes it?

345
00:33:34,354 --> 00:33:36,230
No one was there when Cedric died.

346
00:33:36,397 --> 00:33:39,525
Then read the Prophet,
like your stupid mother.

347
00:33:39,859 --> 00:33:43,071
- Don't insult my mother!
- Don't call me a liar.

348
00:33:43,363 --> 00:33:45,656
- What's wrong?
- He's crazy, that's what happens.

349
00:33:45,990 --> 00:33:48,534
can you believe
What does it say about You-Know-Who?

350
00:33:48,701 --> 00:33:50,703
Yes. I believe him.

351
00:33:51,871 --> 00:33:53,831
Does anyone else have a problem with Harry?

352
00:34:03,049 --> 00:34:05,176
- Are you okay?
- Perfect.

353
00:34:05,635 --> 00:34:08,304
Seamus was very rude, mate.

354
00:34:09,055 --> 00:34:12,934
- But he will come to his senses, you'll see.
- I said I'm fine, Ron!

355
00:34:16,604 --> 00:34:21,234
Sure. I'll leave you alone, then.

356
00:34:49,554 --> 00:34:50,638
<i>Harry-</i>

357
00:35:09,115 --> 00:35:11,659
Come on, Seamus! Come on, hit him!

358
00:35:27,633 --> 00:35:28,926
Good morning, children.

359
00:35:30,845 --> 00:35:36,142
Essential Title Examinations
of Ordinary Magic.

360
00:35:36,350 --> 00:35:38,978
T.I.M.O.S.

361
00:35:39,145 --> 00:35:43,649
Generally known as OWLs.

362
00:35:43,858 --> 00:35:46,944
Study hard and you will be rewarded.

363
00:35:47,278 --> 00:35:52,450
If they don't, the consequences
They can be severe.

364
00:35:58,039 --> 00:36:03,211
Your instruction in this matter
It has been very uneven.

365
00:36:03,419 --> 00:36:05,546
I want you to know that from now on...

366
00:36:05,713 --> 00:36:09,217
...they will follow a very structured course
defensive magic...

367
00:36:09,383 --> 00:36:11,886
...approved by the Ministry.

368
00:36:13,346 --> 00:36:15,515
Is there nothing here about
the use of spells?

369
00:36:15,681 --> 00:36:17,433
The use of spells?

370
00:36:17,892 --> 00:36:21,270
I can't imagine what they need
use spells in my class.

371
00:36:22,897 --> 00:36:26,567
- Aren't we going to use magic?
- They will learn about defensive spells...

372
00:36:26,734 --> 00:36:29,737
...in a risk-free way.

373
00:36:29,904 --> 00:36:32,615
For what?
If they attack us, there will be risks.

374
00:36:32,782 --> 00:36:36,244
The students will raise
the hand to speak!

375
00:36:39,413 --> 00:36:41,916
The Ministry thinks...

376
00:36:42,083 --> 00:36:44,877
...that knowledge
theoretical will be enough...

377
00:36:45,044 --> 00:36:47,004
...so they can pass their exams.

378
00:36:47,171 --> 00:36:49,590
After all, that is
the purpose of teaching.

379
00:36:49,757 --> 00:36:52,593
What use will theory be to us out there?

380
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:54,762
There's nothing out there.

381
00:36:54,929 --> 00:36:57,974
Who do you imagine wants
attack children like you?

382
00:36:58,140 --> 00:37:01,394
I don't know. Maybe Lord Voldemort.

383
00:37:12,196 --> 00:37:15,783
I want to make this perfectly clear.

384
00:37:16,951 --> 00:37:18,619
They have been told...

385
00:37:18,786 --> 00:37:24,083
...that a certain dark wizard
He's lurking again.

386
00:37:24,292 --> 00:37:29,547
- This is a lie.
- It's not! I saw him, I fought with him!

387
00:37:29,714 --> 00:37:33,467
- You are punished, Mr. Potter!
- Did Cedric Diggory die because he wanted to?

388
00:37:33,634 --> 00:37:36,304
The death of Cedric Diggory
It was a tragic accident.

389
00:37:36,470 --> 00:37:38,514
Voldemort murdered him!

390
00:37:38,681 --> 00:37:40,016
Enough!

391
00:37:40,808 --> 00:37:42,393
That's enough.

392
00:37:42,810 --> 00:37:46,689
I want to see it later,
Mr. Potter. In my office.

393
00:38:11,756 --> 00:38:12,882
Go ahead.

394
00:38:18,179 --> 00:38:20,014
Good afternoon, Mr. Potter.

395
00:38:20,765 --> 00:38:21,932
Sit down.

396
00:38:29,649 --> 00:38:32,777
You're going to write me a line, Mr. Potter.

397
00:38:33,861 --> 00:38:35,613
No, not with his pen.

398
00:38:36,113 --> 00:38:38,741
You are going to use a very special pen of mine.

399
00:38:46,624 --> 00:38:52,380
I want you to write:
"I must not tell lies."

400
00:38:54,548 --> 00:38:56,133
How many times?

401
00:38:56,967 --> 00:39:01,055
Let's say until the message penetrates.

402
00:39:03,474 --> 00:39:05,226
He hasn't given me ink.

403
00:39:05,559 --> 00:39:06,811
You won't need it.

404
00:39:42,096 --> 00:39:46,767
I must not tell lies

405
00:39:58,154 --> 00:39:59,655
Yes?

406
00:40:06,954 --> 00:40:10,166
- Nothing.
- Exact.

407
00:40:11,417 --> 00:40:14,628
Because you know, deep down...

408
00:40:15,254 --> 00:40:17,423
...who deserves to be punished.

409
00:40:18,466 --> 00:40:20,301
Right, Mr. Potter?

410
00:40:25,014 --> 00:40:26,640
Continue.

411
00:40:35,524 --> 00:40:37,985
- Class Skipper Assortment.
- Sweets that make you sick.

412
00:40:38,152 --> 00:40:39,779
To get out of class.

413
00:40:39,945 --> 00:40:43,199
Get hours of pleasure
of unproductive tedium.

414
00:40:45,075 --> 00:40:46,076
Do you like another one?

415
00:40:46,243 --> 00:40:48,537
I'm not asking you to write it all down for me.

416
00:40:48,704 --> 00:40:51,791
I am studying
for OWL exams.

417
00:40:52,333 --> 00:40:54,168
I'll write you the introduction and that's it.

418
00:40:54,335 --> 00:40:58,088
You are the most wonderful person
that I have never known.

419
00:40:58,255 --> 00:41:02,343
-And if I'm rude to you again...
- I'll know that you're back to normal.

420
00:41:07,223 --> 00:41:09,517
What do you have in your hand?

421
00:41:10,184 --> 00:41:11,644
Nothing.

422
00:41:12,895 --> 00:41:14,814
The other hand.

423
00:41:17,191 --> 00:41:18,984
Tell Dumbledore.

424
00:41:19,318 --> 00:41:21,529
You already have enough worries.

425
00:41:21,695 --> 00:41:23,823
And I don't want to give Umbridge the pleasure.

426
00:41:23,989 --> 00:41:26,408
Damn. The woman is torturing you.

427
00:41:26,575 --> 00:41:30,287
- If the parents found out...
- I don't have parents, right?

428
00:41:33,332 --> 00:41:35,584
You have to report it.

429
00:41:35,876 --> 00:41:39,255
- It's very simple. You are being...
- No, it's not.

430
00:41:39,547 --> 00:41:42,424
It will be many things, but it is not simple.

431
00:41:43,551 --> 00:41:45,386
You don't understand.

432
00:41:48,180 --> 00:41:49,932
Help us understand.

433
00:42:04,738 --> 00:42:06,365
<i>Dear Canute,</i>

434
00:42:07,241 --> 00:42:08,951
<i>I hope you are well.</i>

435
00:42:09,118 --> 00:42:13,581
<i>It's starting to get cold.
Winter is coming.</i>

436
00:42:16,333 --> 00:42:21,088
<i>Despite being at Hogwarts,
I feel more alone than ever.</i>

437
00:42:21,881 --> 00:42:25,217
<i>I know that you will understand
better than anyone.</i>

438
00:42:59,293 --> 00:43:01,128
Hello, Harry Potter.

439
00:43:04,131 --> 00:43:08,844
- Your feet. Aren't you cold?
- A bit.

440
00:43:09,637 --> 00:43:13,474
But all my shoes
They mysteriously disappeared.

441
00:43:14,183 --> 00:43:17,269
I suspect these are nargles.

442
00:43:23,525 --> 00:43:27,404
- What are they?
- They are called thestrals.

443
00:43:27,821 --> 00:43:33,035
They are very gentle,
but people avoid them because they are...

444
00:43:35,996 --> 00:43:37,706
Different.

445
00:43:40,668 --> 00:43:43,295
Why don't others see them?

446
00:43:43,545 --> 00:43:46,548
Only people see them
who has witnessed death.

447
00:43:48,842 --> 00:43:51,553
So you knew someone who died?

448
00:43:51,720 --> 00:43:53,430
My mom.

449
00:43:53,847 --> 00:43:58,686
She was an extraordinary witch,
but he liked to experiment...

450
00:43:59,019 --> 00:44:02,106
...and one day, a spell went very wrong.

451
00:44:02,398 --> 00:44:04,900
- I was nine years old.
- I'm sorry.

452
00:44:05,526 --> 00:44:07,444
Yes, it was terrible.

453
00:44:07,611 --> 00:44:13,200
Sometimes I feel very sad,
but I have my dad.

454
00:44:15,411 --> 00:44:18,038
We both believe you, by the way.

455
00:44:20,958 --> 00:44:24,128
That He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named
He came back and you fought with him...

456
00:44:24,294 --> 00:44:27,548
...and that the Ministry
and the Prophet conspire against you.

457
00:44:27,715 --> 00:44:28,882
Thank you.

458
00:44:29,383 --> 00:44:31,927
It seems like you are the only ones.

459
00:44:32,094 --> 00:44:33,429
I don't think it's true.

460
00:44:35,556 --> 00:44:38,392
But I guess that's what he wants you to feel.

461
00:44:38,851 --> 00:44:40,352
What do you mean?

462
00:44:41,311 --> 00:44:43,272
If I were You-Know-Who...

463
00:44:43,689 --> 00:44:47,067
...I would like to isolate you from everyone else.

464
00:44:47,317 --> 00:44:50,320
Because if it's just you...

465
00:44:50,988 --> 00:44:53,490
...you're not that big of a threat.

466
00:45:10,924 --> 00:45:15,804
- Do you never stop eating?
- That? I'm hungry.

467
00:45:21,935 --> 00:45:23,687
Can I sit with you?

468
00:45:25,105 --> 00:45:28,317
Forgive me, Professor, but what are you implying?

469
00:45:28,609 --> 00:45:31,361
I only ask that you treat yourself
of my students...

470
00:45:31,528 --> 00:45:35,532
...stick to the measures
common disciplinary measures.

471
00:45:35,949 --> 00:45:37,618
It seems absurd, but it sounds...

472
00:45:37,785 --> 00:45:41,955
...why are you questioning my authority?
in my classroom...

473
00:45:42,122 --> 00:45:43,332
...Minerva.

474
00:45:43,499 --> 00:45:47,961
Not at all, Dolores.
Just your medieval methods.

475
00:45:49,338 --> 00:45:50,798
I'm sorry, dear.

476
00:45:50,964 --> 00:45:54,301
But question my methods
is to question the Ministry...

477
00:45:54,468 --> 00:45:57,513
...and, consequently, to the minister himself.

478
00:45:57,805 --> 00:45:59,389
I am a tolerant woman...

479
00:45:59,556 --> 00:46:04,478
...but the one thing I won't stand
It is disloyalty.

480
00:46:06,396 --> 00:46:08,107
The disloyalty.

481
00:46:09,775 --> 00:46:13,737
Things at Hogwarts are
Much worse than I feared.

482
00:46:13,987 --> 00:46:17,407
Cornelius will want
take immediate action.

483
00:46:21,245 --> 00:46:23,330
DOLORES UMBRIDGE IS NAMED

484
00:46:23,497 --> 00:46:25,666
HOGWARTS HIGH INQUISITOR

485
00:46:25,833 --> 00:46:28,752
MINISTRY UNDERTAKING REFORMS

486
00:46:28,919 --> 00:46:30,838
What happened to Dumbledore?

487
00:46:31,004 --> 00:46:33,549
<i>Having revolutionized...</i>

488
00:46:33,715 --> 00:46:36,385
...the<i>defense teaching
Against the Dark Arts...</i>

489
00:46:37,136 --> 00:46:42,349
<i>...Dolores Umbridge, as Suma
Inquisitor, you will have powers...</i>

490
00:46:43,183 --> 00:46:48,147
...to correct educational deterioration
from Hogwarts School.

491
00:46:55,904 --> 00:46:58,031
Just one question, dear.

492
00:46:58,198 --> 00:47:02,411
How long have you been in this position?

493
00:47:09,334 --> 00:47:14,214
Did you apply for the Defense position?
Against the Dark Arts?

494
00:47:14,590 --> 00:47:16,592
Yes.

495
00:47:17,009 --> 00:47:19,428
But you didn't succeed?

496
00:47:20,762 --> 00:47:23,056
Obviously.

497
00:47:41,909 --> 00:47:44,036
PROHIBITED MUSIC
WHILE STUDYING

498
00:47:44,203 --> 00:47:46,538
PROHIBITED WEASLEY PRODUCTS

499
00:47:46,705 --> 00:47:48,707
APPROPRIATE CLOTHING AND BEHAVIOR

500
00:47:55,631 --> 00:47:58,926
Can you predict something for me, please?

